Subject: fix(config): allow the configured forge in the default remote-resource allowlist

The CLI resolves fullsend-ai/agents and fullsend-ai/fullsend against
GITHUB_SERVER_URL, and an enterprise host serves raw content from itself at
<host>/<owner>/<repo>/raw/<ref>/<path> rather than from
raw.githubusercontent.com. The default allowed_remote_resources named only the
two public prefixes, so on such a host every URL the CLI builds was refused by
its own allowlist:

  Error: resolving agent "triage": remote resource not allowed

and a config scaffolded there by `admin install` carried the refusal into the
repository, where the first run failed until someone edited the list by hand.

Derive two more prefixes, for the same two repositories on the configured
forge, from the variable that already decides where the fetches go. Every
caller of the default benefits: the scaffold writes them, EnsureDefault merges
them into an existing config at run time, and the lock and enumerate fallbacks
see them. Anything on github.com keeps the two public prefixes and nothing
else, so behaviour there is unchanged.

Breadboard note: patches Go source, so it belongs to the build patch list in
deploy/scripts/05i-build-fullsend.sh. It replaces deploy/fullsend/seed/
seed-config-allowlist.py, which appended the local prefix after the scaffold
merged. Written to be sent upstream as-is. Add a DCO sign-off before
submitting it as a human-authored change.

diff --git a/internal/config/config.go b/internal/config/config.go
index 7ec2138..dce9e59 100644
--- a/internal/config/config.go
+++ b/internal/config/config.go
@@ -2,6 +2,8 @@ package config
 
 import (
 	"fmt"
+	"net/url"
+	"os"
 	"path"
 	"regexp"
 	"slices"
@@ -440,12 +442,50 @@ func PerRepoDefaultRoles() []string {
 }
 
 // DefaultAllowedRemoteResources returns the standard allowlist prefixes
-// for base composition and agent registration URLs.
+// for base composition and agent registration URLs: the public raw hosts
+// for the two first-party repositories, plus the same two repositories on
+// the configured forge when that forge is not github.com.
+//
+// The CLI resolves those repositories against GITHUB_SERVER_URL, and an
+// enterprise host serves raw content from itself at
+// <host>/<owner>/<repo>/raw/<ref>/<path> rather than from
+// raw.githubusercontent.com. An allowlist naming only the public hosts then
+// refuses every URL the CLI builds there, including the harness it needs to
+// run at all; and a config scaffolded on such a host carried that refusal
+// into the repository. Deriving the prefixes from the same variable keeps
+// the allowlist consistent with where the fetches go. Anything on github.com
+// keeps the two public prefixes and nothing else, so behaviour there is
+// unchanged.
 func DefaultAllowedRemoteResources() []string {
-	return []string{
+	resources := []string{
 		"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fullsend-ai/fullsend/",
 		"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/fullsend-ai/agents/",
 	}
+	if server := configuredForgeServer(); server != "" {
+		resources = append(resources,
+			server+"/fullsend-ai/fullsend/",
+			server+"/fullsend-ai/agents/",
+		)
+	}
+	return resources
+}
+
+// configuredForgeServer returns GITHUB_SERVER_URL without a trailing slash
+// when it names a host other than github.com, and "" otherwise.
+func configuredForgeServer() string {
+	server := strings.TrimRight(strings.TrimSpace(os.Getenv("GITHUB_SERVER_URL")), "/")
+	if server == "" {
+		return ""
+	}
+	parsed, err := url.Parse(server)
+	if err != nil || parsed.Host == "" {
+		return ""
+	}
+	host := strings.ToLower(parsed.Hostname())
+	if host == "github.com" || strings.HasSuffix(host, ".github.com") {
+		return ""
+	}
+	return server
 }
 
